 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the town of Warwick, county of Orange to alienate certain\nlands held in public trust in the town of Warwick, county of Orange",
    "basePrintNo": "S6755",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6755-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6755\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing the town of Warwick, county of Orange to alienate\ncertain lands held in public trust in the town of Warwick, county of\nOrange\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the town of Warwick to discontinue public trust lands and\nalienate them to urbanXtracts, a cannabis business, in exchange for\nlands more suitable for recreational public park use and for the town to\ndedicate an amount equal to or greater than the fair market value of the\nproperty being alienated to the acquisition of new lands or capital\nimprovements to existing lands held in public trust for recreation,\nhistoric and/or environmental preservation purposes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: The town of Warwick is authorized to discontinue certain\npublic trust lands and sell them to urbanXtracts, a cannabis business,\nfor the purpose of exchanging the land for other land that is better\nsuited for recreational public park use.\n\nSection 2: The authorization in Section 1 is conditional upon the town\nof Warwick dedicating an amount equal to or greater than the fair market\nvalue of the land being sold towards either acquiring new lands for\npublic use or improving existing lands held in public trust.\n\nSection 3: Describes the specific parcel of land that the town of\nWarwick is authorized to discontinue and sell to urbanXtracts under the\nconditions outlined in Sections 1 and 2.\n\nSection 4: States that if the town of Warwick receives any funding or\nassistance from the federal government for the purchase, maintenance, or\nimprovement of the lands held in public trust, then the discontinuance\nand alienation of such lands held in public trust, as authorized in\nsection one of the act, cannot occur until the town of Warwick complies\nwith any federal requirements related to the alienation or conversion of\nsuch public trust lands.\n\nSection 5: Sets effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill will allow the town of Warwick, in Orange County, New York, to\ndiscontinue public trust lands and exchange them with private lands\nowned by a cannabis business called urban tracts. This exchange of lands\nwill allow for the development of recreational public park use, which\nare more suitable for this purpose and are adjacent to an existing town\npark. This exchange will also require the town to dedicate an amount\nequal to or greater than the fair market value of the property being\nalienated towards the acquisition of new lands or capital improvements\nto existing lands held in public trust for recreation, historic, and\nenvironmental preservation purposes. The bill is needed to enable the\ntown to make this exchange and ensure that the public trust lands are\nused effectively for public purposes.\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nEffective Immediately.\n",
